{"pinyin":"lì","traditional":"力","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zú","traditional":"足","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"modern":"盖","pinyin":"gài","traditional":"蓋","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"wǒ","traditional":"我","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"未","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"见","pinyin":"jiàn","traditional":"見","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Aku belum pernah melihat orang yang benar-benar menyukai Cinta Kasih dan benar-benar membenci laku yang tidak Cinta Kasih. Seorang yang benar-benar menyukai Cinta Kasih, tidak ada hal lain yang lebih dimuliakan daripadanya. Seorang yang benar-benar membenci laku yang tidak Cinta Kasih selalu berusaha melaksanakan Cinta Kasih sedemikian rupa, sehingga tidak memungkinkan barang sesuatu yang tidak berperi Cinta Kasih melekat pada dirinya. (2) Bila suatu hari seseorang mengerahkan seluruh kekuatannya dalam Cinta Kasih, Aku belum pernah melihat ia akan kekurangan tenaga. Mungkin ada juga, tetapi Aku belum pernah melihatnya.\"","translation_english":"1. The Master said, 'I have not seen a person who loved virtue, or one who hated what was not virtuous. He who loved virtue, would esteem nothing above it. He who hated what is not virtuous, would practise virtue in such a way that he would not allow anything that is not virtuous to approach his person. 2. 'Is any one able for one day to apply his strength to virtue? I have not seen the case in which his strength would be insufficient. 3. 'Should there possibly be any such case, I have not seen it.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.07","number":7,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"过","pinyin":"guò","traditional":"過","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"gè","traditional":"各","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"qí","traditional":"其","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"党","pinyin":"dǎng","traditional":"黨","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"modern":"观","pinyin":"guān","traditional":"觀","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"过","pinyin":"guò","traditional":"過","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"sī","traditional":"斯","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"仁","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Adapun kesalahan seseorang itu masing-masing sesuai dengan sifatnya. Bahkan dari kesalahannya dapat diketahui apakah ia seorang yang berperi Cinta Kasih.\" (S.S. I: 8).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'The faults of men are characteristic of the class to which they belong. By observing a man's faults, it may be known that he is virtuous.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.08","number":8,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"cháo","traditional":"朝","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"闻","pinyin":"wén","traditional":"聞","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"xī","traditional":"夕","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"sǐ","traditional":"死","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Pagi mendengar akan Jalan Suci, sore hari matipun ikhlas.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'If a man in the morning hear the right way, he may die in the evening without regret.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.09","number":9,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"shì","traditional":"士","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhì","traditional":"志","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"耻","pinyin":"chǐ","traditional":"恥","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"恶","pinyin":"è","traditional":"惡","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yī","traditional":"衣","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"恶","pinyin":"è","traditional":"惡","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shí","traditional":"食","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"未","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zú","traditional":"足","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yǔ","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"议","pinyin":"yì","traditional":"議","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang siswa yang benar-benar hendak hidup di dalam Jalan Suci, tetapi masih malu berpakaian buruk dan makan tidak enak, sesungguhnya ia belum masuk hitungan.\" (S.S. XIV: 2).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'A scholar, whose mind is set on truth, and who is ashamed of bad clothes and bad food, is not fit to be discoursed with.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.10","number":10,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"tiān","traditional":"天","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xià","traditional":"下","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"适","pinyin":"shì","traditional":"適","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mò","traditional":"莫","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"义","pinyin":"yì","traditional":"義","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"与","pinyin":"yǔ","traditional":"與","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bǐ","traditional":"比","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang Junzi - Kuncu terhadap persoalan di dunia tidak mengiakan atau menolak mentah-mentah. Hanya Kebenaranlah yang dijadikan ukuran.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'The superior man, in the world, does not set his mind either for anything, or against anything; what is right he will follow.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.11","number":11,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"怀","pinyin":"huái","traditional":"懷","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dé","traditional":"德","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"xiǎo","traditional":"小","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"怀","pinyin":"huái","traditional":"懷","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"tǔ","traditional":"土","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"怀","pinyin":"huái","traditional":"懷","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xíng","traditional":"刑","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"xiǎo","traditional":"小","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"怀","pinyin":"huái","traditional":"懷","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"huì","traditional":"惠","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang Junzi - Kuncu senantiasa ingat akan Kebajikan, sedangkan seorang rendah budi hanya ingat kenikmatan; seorang Junzi - Kuncu senantiasa ingat akan hukum, sedangkan seorang rendah budi hanya mengharapkan belas kasihan orang.\" (S.S. XIV: 2).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'The superior man thinks of virtue; the small man thinks of comfort. The superior man thinks of the sanctions of law; the small man thinks of favours which he may receive.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.12","number":12,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"fàng","traditional":"放","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"lì","traditional":"利","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xíng","traditional":"行","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"duō","traditional":"多","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuàn","traditional":"怨","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang yang hanya mengejar keuntungan saja, niscaya banyak yang menyesalkan.\" (A.B. X: 23).","translation_english":"The Master said: 'He who acts with a constant view to his own advantage will be much murmured against.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.13","number":13,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"néng","traditional":"能","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"礼","pinyin":"lǐ","traditional":"禮","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"让","pinyin":"ràng","traditional":"讓","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"为","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"為","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"国","pinyin":"guó","traditional":"國","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？"},{"pinyin":"hé","traditional":"何","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"néng","traditional":"能","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"礼","pinyin":"lǐ","traditional":"禮","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"让","pinyin":"ràng","traditional":"讓","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"为","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"為","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"国","pinyin":"guó","traditional":"國","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"rú","traditional":"如","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"礼","pinyin":"lǐ","traditional":"禮","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hé","traditional":"何","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Bila orang dapat menggunakan Kesusilaan dan Kerendahan Hati di dalam mengatur negara, apakah kesukarannya? Kalau tidak dapat menggunakan Kesusilaan dan Kerendahan Hati di dalam mengatur negara, apakah guna Kesusilaan?\" (S.S. I: 12).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'Is a prince is able to govern his kingdom with the complaisance proper to the rules of propriety, what difficulty will he have? If he cannot govern it with that complaisance, what has he to do with the rules of propriety?'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.14","number":14,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"huàn","traditional":"患","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"位","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"huàn","traditional":"患","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"suǒ","traditional":"所","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"lì","traditional":"立","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"huàn","traditional":"患","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mò","traditional":"莫","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jǐ","traditional":"己","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"qiú","traditional":"求","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"为","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"為","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Janganlah khawatir tiada kedudukan, berkhawatirlah kalau tidak mempunyai kecakapan untuk suatu kedudukan; janganlah khawatir tiada orang yang mengetahui dirimu, tetapi berusahalah agar mempunyai kecakapan yang patut diketahui.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'A man should say, I am not concerned that I have no place, I am concerned how I may fit myself for one. I am not concerned that I am not known, I seek to be worthy to be known.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.15","number":15,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"modern":"参","pinyin":"cān","traditional":"參","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"hū","traditional":"乎","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"！"},{"pinyin":"wú","traditional":"吾","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yī","traditional":"一","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贯","pinyin":"guàn","traditional":"貫","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"},{"pinyin":"céng","traditional":"曾","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"wéi","traditional":"唯","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"chū","traditional":"出","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"门","pinyin":"mén","traditional":"門","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"问","pinyin":"wèn","traditional":"問","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"hé","traditional":"何","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谓","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"謂","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"？”"},{"pinyin":"céng","traditional":"曾","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"fū","traditional":"夫","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"zhōng","traditional":"忠","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shù","traditional":"恕","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"已","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Cham, ketahuilah, Jalan SuciKu itu satu, tetapi menembusi semuanya.\" Zengzi - Cingcu menjawab, \"Ya, Guru.\" (2) Setelah Nabi pergi, murid-murid lain bertanya, \"Apakah maksud kata-kata tadi?\" (A.B. X 1,2; T.S. XII S.S. VI: 30; XII: 2; XV: 3). (3) Zengzi - Cingcu menjawab, \"Jalan Suci Guru, tidak lebih tidak kurang ialah Satya dan tepasarira.\" (T.S. XII 4).","translation_english":"1. The Master said, 'Shan, my doctrine is that of an all-pervading unity.' The disciple Tsang replied, 'Yes.' 2. The Master went out, and the other disciples asked, saying, 'What do his words mean?' Tsang said, 'The doctrine of our master is to be true to the principles of our nature and the benevolent exercise of them to others,-- this and nothing more.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.16","number":16,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yù","traditional":"喻","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"义","pinyin":"yì","traditional":"義","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"xiǎo","traditional":"小","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rén","traditional":"人","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yù","traditional":"喻","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"lì","traditional":"利","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang Junzi - Kuncu hanya mengerti akan Kebenaran, sebaliknya seorang rendah budi hanya mengerti akan keuntungan.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'The mind of the superior man is conversant with righteousness; the mind of the mean man is conversant with gain.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.17","number":17,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"modern":"见","pinyin":"jiàn","traditional":"見","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贤","pinyin":"xián","traditional":"賢","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"sī","traditional":"思","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"齐","pinyin":"qí","traditional":"齊","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yān","traditional":"焉","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"见","pinyin":"jiàn","traditional":"見","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"贤","pinyin":"xián","traditional":"賢","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"内","pinyin":"nèi","traditional":"內","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zì","traditional":"自","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shěng","traditional":"省","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Bila melihat seorang yang Bijaksana, berusahalah menyamainya; dan, bila melihat seorang yang tidak Bijaksana, periksalah dirimu sendiri.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'When we see men of worth, we should think of equalling them; when we see men of a contrary character, we should turn inwards and examine ourselves.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.18","number":18,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"shì","traditional":"事","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"父","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mǔ","traditional":"母","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"几","pinyin":"jǐ","traditional":"幾","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谏","pinyin":"jiàn","traditional":"諫","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"见","pinyin":"jiàn","traditional":"見","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhì","traditional":"志","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"从","pinyin":"cóng","traditional":"從","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"yòu","traditional":"又","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jìng","traditional":"敬","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"违","pinyin":"wéi","traditional":"違","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"劳","pinyin":"láo","traditional":"勞","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuàn","traditional":"怨","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Di dalam melayani ayah bunda, boleh memperingatkan (tetapi hendaklah lemah lembut). Bila tidak diturut, bersikaplah lebih hormat dan janganlah melanggar. Meskipun harus bercapai lelah, janganlah menggerutu.\" (S.S. XX: 2).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'In serving his parents, a son may remonstrate with them, but gently; when he sees that they do not incline to follow his advice, he shows an increased degree of reverence, but does not abandon his purpose; and should they punish him, he does not allow himself to murmur.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.19","number":19,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"父","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mǔ","traditional":"母","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zài","traditional":"在","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"远","pinyin":"yuǎn","traditional":"遠","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yóu","traditional":"游","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"yóu","traditional":"游","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bì","traditional":"必","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"fāng","traditional":"方","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Pada saat orang tua masih hidup, janganlah jauh mengembara. Bila terpaksa mengembara, haruslah mempunyai tujuan yang tertentu.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'While his parents are alive, the son may not go abroad to a distance. If he does go abroad, he must have a fixed place to which he goes.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.20","number":20,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"sān","traditional":"三","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"nián","traditional":"年","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"无","pinyin":"wú","traditional":"無","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"gǎi","traditional":"改","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"父","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dào","traditional":"道","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"谓","pinyin":"wèi","traditional":"謂","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xiào","traditional":"孝","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Bila seseorang selama tiga tahun tidak mengubah Jalan Suci ayahnya, bolehlah ia dinamai berbakti.\" (S.S. I: 11).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'If the son for three years does not alter from the way of his father, he may be called filial.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.21","number":21,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"fù","traditional":"父","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mǔ","traditional":"母","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"nián","traditional":"年","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"kě","traditional":"可","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"知","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。"},{"pinyin":"yī","traditional":"一","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"则","pinyin":"zé","traditional":"則","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xǐ","traditional":"喜","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"yī","traditional":"一","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"则","pinyin":"zé","traditional":"則","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"惧","pinyin":"jù","traditional":"懼","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Usia ayah bunda tidak boleh tidak diketahui; di satu pihak boleh merasa gembira, di lain pihak harus merasa khawatir.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'The years of parents may by no means not be kept in the memory, as an occasion at once for joy and for fear.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.22","number":22,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"gǔ","traditional":"古","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yán","traditional":"言","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"chū","traditional":"出","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"modern":"耻","pinyin":"chǐ","traditional":"恥","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"gōng","traditional":"躬","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"dǎi","traditional":"逮","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yě","traditional":"也","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Adapun sebabnya orang jaman dahulu merasa sukar mengucapkan kata- kata, ialah karena merasa malu kalau tidak dapat melaksanakannya.\" (S.S. XIV: 20).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'The reason why the ancients did not readily give utterance to their words, was that they feared lest their actions should not come up to them.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.23","number":23,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"以","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"约","pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"約","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shī","traditional":"失","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhī","traditional":"之","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zhě","traditional":"者","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"鲜","pinyin":"xiān","traditional":"鮮","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seseorang yang dapat membatasi dirinya, sekalipun mungkin berbuat salah, pasti jaranglah terjadi.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'The cautious seldom err.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.24","number":24,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yù","traditional":"欲","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"讷","pinyin":"nè","traditional":"訥","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yán","traditional":"言","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"ér","traditional":"而","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"mǐn","traditional":"敏","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"于","pinyin":"yú","traditional":"於","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"xíng","traditional":"行","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Seorang Junzi - Kuncu lambat bicara tetapi tangkas bekerja.\" (S.S. XIII: 27).","translation_english":"The Master said, 'The superior man wishes to be slow in his speech and earnest in his conduct.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.25","number":25,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"dé","traditional":"德","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"bù","traditional":"不","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"gū","traditional":"孤","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"bì","traditional":"必","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"有","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"邻","pinyin":"lín","traditional":"鄰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Nabi bersabda, \"Kebajikan tidak akan terpencil, ia pasti beroleh tetangga.\"","translation_english":"The Master said, 'Virtue is not left to stand alone. He who practises it will have neighbors.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"},{"editorial_status":"unverified-draft","id":"sishu.lunyu.04.26","number":26,"ruby_paragraphs":[[{"pinyin":"zǐ","traditional":"子","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yóu","traditional":"游","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yuē","traditional":"曰","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"：“"},{"pinyin":"shì","traditional":"事","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"jūn","traditional":"君","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"数","pinyin":"shù","traditional":"數","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"sī","traditional":"斯","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"rǔ","traditional":"辱","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"；"},{"pinyin":"péng","traditional":"朋","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǒu","traditional":"友","type":"ruby"},{"modern":"数","pinyin":"shù","traditional":"數","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"，"},{"pinyin":"sī","traditional":"斯","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"shū","traditional":"疏","type":"ruby"},{"pinyin":"yǐ","traditional":"矣","type":"ruby"},{"type":"text","value":"。”"}]],"translation_indonesian":"Cu-yu berkata, \"Dalam mengabdi kepada pemimpin bila berkali-kali memperingatkan, niscaya akan beroleh malu. Dalam bersahabat, bila berkali-kali memperingatkan, niscaya akan renggang.\" SABDA SUCI JILID V. KONG-YA TIANG","translation_english":"Tsze-yu said, 'In serving a prince, frequent remonstrances lead to disgrace. Between friends, frequent reproofs make the friendship distant.'","translation_english_source":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/4094","translation_english_alignment":"chapter-count-exact; needs editorial collation"}],"source_file":"03 - Lun Yu 論語/04 - Jilid IV - Li Ren (Cinta Kasih) - 里仁篇.md","title":"Jilid IV — Li Ren (Cinta Kasih) · 里仁篇"}
